course: dictionary
lesson: 13101
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can find out which meaning fits by reading the words around it. «The mixture in the glass was fizzing.» Here the clues are the glass and the mixture, so fizzing means making lots of small bubbles.
explain: The same word can describe a feeling. «Tom was fizzing with ideas for his story.» Nobody is bubbling here. The words with ideas tell you that fizzing means full of energy and excitement.
explain: In UK slang, fizzing can mean very angry. «Mum was fizzing when she saw the muddy boots.» Ask yourself: does this sentence make sense with bubbles? No. Then try the other meaning and see if it fits better.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Fizzing» can mean making bubbles with a hissing sound.
fact: «Fizzing» can mean full of energy or excitement, as in «fizzing with ideas».
fact: In UK and Irish informal speech, «fizzing» can mean very angry.
fact: To check the meaning, swap your idea into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The mixture in the glass was fizzing.» What does fizzing mean here? | Melting into a puddle | Very quiet and still | Frozen solid | *Making lots of small bubbles with a hissing sound
exercise: «Tom was fizzing with ideas for his story.» What does fizzing suggest? | Very quiet | *Full of energy and excitement | Cold and wet | Tired and sleepy
exercise: In the UK, a friend says, «Mum was fizzing when she saw the muddy boots.» What does fizzing mean? | Laughing loudly | *Very angry | Making bubbles | Feeling sick
test: What sound does a fizzing drink make? | *A hissing sound | A loud bang like a drum | A soft hum | Complete silence
test: Which word could replace fizzing in «She was fizzing with excitement»? | Silent | *Bursting with energy | Freezing | Dripping
exam: In a science experiment, why does a fizzing mixture matter? | *It shows a gas is being made | It means the lab is closed | It shows the mixture is cold | It means the experiment has finished
